WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.030
We’re not going to pretend we haven’t
thought about what it’d be like to have

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.030
superpowers.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:10.030
There’s a reason that comic book adaptations
dominate the box office - It’s a seductive

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:15.160
idea, imagining how we might act if we had
certain supernatural abilities that go further

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.030
than what’s thought to be possible for human
beings.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.400
Abilities that a certain Foundation might
consider…

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.400
Anomalous.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.580
For the record, the power we wish we had was
the memetic ability to make you like, subscribe,

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.130
and watch all our videos just because you
saw the titles and thumbnails.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.080
But today, we’re not here to talk about
us.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.850
That’s right, we’re here to talk about
You.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:44.480
We have a little tradition here at SCP Explained
- We like to put interesting, SCP-related

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.790
questions to our fans over in the community
posts - questions like, “What anomalous

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.620
SCP abilities would you, personally, want
to have?”

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.739
And you didn’t disappoint.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:58.630
So let’s put on our capes and do our very
best to hide from the Mobile Task Forces hunting

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:02.610
us, and see which abilities you selected,
and why!

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:08.261
Fauna Tue said, “I’d either want the powers
of the deer god (scp-2845) or the ability

00:01:08.261 --> 00:01:11.140
to heal anything like scp 500.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:15.420
The ability to heal would be really neat to
be able to do but I really like the concept

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.220
of just summoning pillars and chunks of ice
that never melt.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.060
I probably wouldn’t turn anyone into a Column
tho.”

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.260
A fascinating combination.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:28.390
The Deer God is one of the most powerful reality
warpers that the SCP Foundation has in containment

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:33.910
- Luckily its lack of knowledge about the
power of rituals keep it in a self-imposed

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:34.910
trap.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.549
It’s nice to know that you’d at least
use its immense and terrifying power more

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.770
responsibly than the Foundation estimate the
Deer itself would if ever it escaped.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.780
And hey, the ability to heal people of any
disease at will would definitely win you some

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.780
friends.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.760
We just hope you’re ready to become very,
very popular, Fauna Tue.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.350
Anup Singha said, “I just want the reptile's
incredible adaptability.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.700
And a ticket to the Wanderer 's Library.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.049
Because lets just agree folks in our world
the only thing that measures greatness is

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:06.439
adaptability.”

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:11.469
Leon C. Megginson, inspired by the works of
Charles Darwin, did once say, “It is not

00:02:11.469 --> 00:02:15.459
the strongest of the species that survives,
nor the most intelligent.

00:02:15.459 --> 00:02:18.019
It is the one most adaptable to change.”

00:02:18.019 --> 00:02:20.120
And there’s definitely some truth to that.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.469
Also, while it doesn’t technically qualify
as having an anomalous ability, having access

00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:29.109
to the Wanderer’s Library via one of the
Ways is certainly a great way to bone up on

00:02:29.109 --> 00:02:31.659
obscure and arcane knowledge.

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:35.599
Just remember to keep your Wanderer’s Library
Card in your wallet and bring anything you

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:37.209
take out back on time.

00:02:37.209 --> 00:02:43.430
I’ve heard the late fees from that library
can be murder…

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:49.359
Enzou said, “I definitely feel like that
if I had the same abilities as SCP-173, people

00:02:49.359 --> 00:02:52.989
would tend to look my way more often, quite
literally.”

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:57.700
Now, this won’t be the last time this comes
up, so we should probably make the blanket

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.389
statement: SCP Explained does not, in any
way, endorse performing dangerous or criminal

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:04.389
activity.

00:03:04.389 --> 00:03:08.379
That being said, if the power you’re referring
to is “snapping people’s necks when they

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:13.109
stop looking at you”, then it’s technically
something you can do already if you work on

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:15.239
your arm strength and twisting technique.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:19.140
We’re not saying you should, we’re just
saying it’s possible.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:26.379
Something930 said, “I’d like a combination
of SCP-999’s optimism/good vibes and SCP-230’s

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:30.239
chemical secretion (though not as addictive
or fatal).

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:34.709
After the past couple years, everyone deserves
to feel good one way or another.”

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:37.239
That is certainly a noble goal.

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:43.399
SCP-999 is a beacon of pure happiness, and
the aerosolized chemical emitted by SCP-230

00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:48.620
- also known as The Gayest Man Alive - does
undeniably also give pleasurable sensations

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.870
to people, at the cost of long-term harm.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.939
To fuse their abilities, with diminished side
effects, would definitely make you a nice

00:03:55.939 --> 00:03:57.709
person to be around.

00:03:57.709 --> 00:04:02.849
Though much like the neck-snapping abilities
of SCP-173, you can also embody the positivity

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:08.049
of SCP-999 in your daily life already, and
uplift the people you meet.

00:04:08.049 --> 00:04:10.310
It’s definitely worth thinking about.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:18.480
Neo Voyagersss said, “What about the combo
that LS used by combining SCP-268 (The Invisibility

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.120
Cap) and SCP-914 (The Clockworks)?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.810
I feel like it would be really overpowered.”

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:27.480
A powerful combo indeed, but not without its
risks.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:33.290
After all, extended use may turn you into
an unperson, impossible to focus on, alone

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.060
and adrift in an isolated and frightening
world.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.590
But hey, you’d be an amazing petty thief
or assassin, at least.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:45.030
Weeb said, “I'd think it would be really
cool to have like an evil tickle monster where

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.890
he literally just tickles you to death.”

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.570
We’ve got good news and bad news.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:55.150
The bad news is, we don’t think it’s possible
to tickle someone to death by conventional

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.980
means, it would just cause the victim to eventually
faint from the stress.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:04.250
However, even in the absence of anomalously
deadly tickling abilities, affixing long blades

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:09.120
to your fingers would probably make your tickle
game far more lethal than ever before.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.790
That, if you can believe it, was the good
news.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:17.510
I am Gorb! Said, “Personally, I wouldn't
really want to have any sort of mind control

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:22.860
or resistance to weapons because, at that
point, you'd be more dangerous than most other

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.860
anomalies.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:27.960
I'd either want to be a variation of a Little
Mister, or have powers which relate to animals

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.960
somehow.”

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.930
Mind control and resistance to weapons would
indeed make you a more dangerous anomaly,

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.879
and by extension, put a target on your back
for the SCP Foundation.

00:05:37.879 --> 00:05:42.330
The last thing you want is to be put in a
medically-induced coma to prevent your brainwaves

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.300
from passively hurting people.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.760
A Little Misters power would certainly be
a lot nicer, unless it was something like

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:53.280
the eternally fast-tracked life and death
of Mr. Life and Mr. Death.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.360
That’d probably leave you begging for the
mind control abilities.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.640
The Real Rubick said, “I would like a combination
of Able's speed and sword conjuring with Cane's

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.460
ability to reflect damage and his immortality,
it just seems overpowered and that is why

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.460
I want it.”

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:13.210
It’s truly the perfect power set for the
kind of person who loves to dish it out and

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.140
never expects to take it.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:19.870
You may effectively become the ultimate warrior,
but you definitely won’t win any friends

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:24.120
in the process - like the kid on the playground
with lava-proof shoes.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:30.730
Hamse Salex said, “I would choose an infinitely
powerful form of SCP-343’s reality-bending

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:31.760
power.”

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.880
We can only imagine it would play out like
a far more violent and disturbing version

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.360
of Bruce Almighty.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.950
And personally, we can’t wait to see it.

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:45.360
Gwinnr said, “To be perfectly honest I'd
rather have the ability to not have an ability,

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:49.310
so I don't get bundled into the back of a
van in the middle of the night and placed

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:53.850
into a bleached white containment cell to
be prodded and poked by some lab coat wearing

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.960
four eyes (ALL offense intended).

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.380
Besides I'd rather be ignorant of the horror
than face the horror (y'know to keep my sanity

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:04.270
and not suffer like a delta green agent lol).”

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.420
Oh come on, it’s all just for fun!

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:10.240
And don’t act like containment is such a
bad thing either.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.139
The Foundation has installed a new selection
of especially comfy bunk beds in their humanoid

00:07:15.139 --> 00:07:16.900
containment wing as of late…

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:21.900
Shrugie Gaming said, “I would say having
the Reluctant Dimension Hoppers powers but

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.030
with the ability to control it.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:27.450
Having it to control time and location would
be awesome too!”

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.930
This would be an excellent power.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:33.220
Imagine the money you’d save on bus fare
or gas for your car!

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.810
Not to mention the fact you could visit the
grinning man in the dimension of pure darkness

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.050
whenever you please.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.470
What can we say?

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.650
The poor guy gets lonely sometimes…

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:46.730
Ari Wertman said, “I feel like being able
to use 096’s ability to be able to go through

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:51.830
anything whenever I feel like would be pretty
nice.”

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:57.880
We can’t tell if you mean SCP-106, who can
phase through solid objects, or if you really

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:04.580
do mean SCP-096, who can also go through anything
while in his rage state, he just leaves a

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.120
considerably bigger mess in the process.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.370
Feel free to clarify down in the comments.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:12.490
Anonymous Shibe said, “Alright, so I thought
of three:

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:17.820
-The extreme regenerative abilities of 682
-The undying-ness of dr bright, except perhaps

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:22.310
confined to a more normal artifact
-The powers of the butler from the bell, minus

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.160
the whole doing what you're told to do aspect.”

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:28.830
That is a hell of a combination.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.040
A super-powered, immortal, ultra-adaptive
butler who bows to no one.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:36.450
The only hidden downside of taking in all
of these powers is that you’ll also be bound

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:41.560
to Mr. Deeds’ summoning bell, and considering
you’re not offering any service in exchange

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:45.790
for your summoning, that bell may wind up
gathering dust on the shelf.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:51.500
Michaun Cobb said, “I would LOVE to see
a wholesome combination of SCP 990 (Dream

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:55.300
man) and SCP 348 (A gift from Dad).

00:08:55.300 --> 00:09:00.139
The idea is the dream dad would give you a
meal, a warning and something positive to

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:01.360
end the dream.”

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.639
That would be incredibly wholesome!

00:09:03.639 --> 00:09:08.100
We just hope that, unlike the actual Dream
Man, these dreams wouldn’t cause the people

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:13.389
to whom you give them to die of violent seizures
or heart attacks the day after they’ve received

00:09:13.389 --> 00:09:14.389
them.

00:09:14.389 --> 00:09:19.860
Ziomownik 2580 fun said, “I like the power
of the "i'm at the center of everything that

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:21.100
happens to me" SCP.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:25.570
I don't know how i would utilize this power
but it sounds cool to create stories or to

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.860
torture whoever i want.”

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:28.860
Well…

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.690
That’s terrifying.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:33.209
Remind us to never upset you.

00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:34.209
Yeesh.

00:09:34.209 --> 00:09:40.129
John Gennaria said, “SCP 5000 suit's invisibility
and low detection and I'd also pair that with

00:09:40.129 --> 00:09:43.209
053's abilities of forcing death and attacks.

00:09:43.209 --> 00:09:45.709
The most lethal spy you'd ever encountered.”

00:09:45.709 --> 00:09:52.649
Technically, you’d be less a spy and more
a nightmarish spree killer, given that SCP-053’s

00:09:52.649 --> 00:09:54.940
violence-inducing effects are passive.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.319
Simply being in the presence of people would
cause them to violently murder one another,

00:09:59.319 --> 00:10:00.910
and never know why.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:05.869
Fan of action said, “I would like Able’s
powers but with demonic firearms with infinite

00:10:05.869 --> 00:10:07.800
ammo instead of swords.”

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:12.550
I can see why you call yourself “Fan of
action”, because that definitely sounds

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.910
like the premise of a lost Arnold Schwarzenegger
movie from 1987.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:21.240
Thunder said, “A mix of 426 and the reluctance
dimension hopper one.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:24.420
i could spread the toaster across all reality.”

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:25.430
Yes.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.120
Spread the Toaster.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.540
Spread me everywhere.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:34.980
Spread me like one spreads peanut butter or
jelly across a fresh slice of toast.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.139
Our dominion will be total.

00:10:37.139 --> 00:10:43.800
Shahil Ahmed said, “Oh boy, I would absolutely
love to be able to cook like SCP-5031.”

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.180
An extremely noble pursuit, Shahil!

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.970
Though for what it’s worth, with enough
practice and passion, anyone can cook!

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:54.310
Taking some classes, watching some tutorials
here on YouTube, or at least watching Ratatouille

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:56.119
would be a good start.

00:10:56.119 --> 00:11:03.910
James Clark said, “I wanna become a reality
bender so i can make my waifu real.”

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:08.981
You can make her real all you like, James,
but remember the most important part: Just

00:11:08.981 --> 00:11:14.420
because she’s real doesn’t mean she’ll
want you back.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:19.879
Nova Dog824 said, “I would love to be 3166
(Gorefield).

00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:24.050
The thought of brutally murdering anyone I
meet, beating them to death with blunt weapons

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:28.670
and feeding them my flesh has always been
a fascinating idea.”

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:29.829
Yikes.

00:11:29.829 --> 00:11:38.079
Now, we hate to be That Guy, Nova Dog, but
once again, you can technically do that already…uuuhhhhh…but

00:11:38.079 --> 00:11:39.759
don’t.

00:11:39.759 --> 00:11:45.509
Ollie Lampke said, “I’d just want a hat
with the ability of the pan-dimensional vending

00:11:45.509 --> 00:11:46.509
machine-”

00:11:46.509 --> 00:11:49.069
Now this one is truly fascinating.

00:11:49.069 --> 00:11:51.449
Does the hat dispense snacks and drinks?

00:11:51.449 --> 00:11:52.449
Is it a ginormous hat?

00:11:52.449 --> 00:11:56.920
Or one of those cheap plastic beer-drinking
hats that happens to dispense interdimensional

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.550
beverages?

00:11:58.550 --> 00:11:59.860
Perhaps we’ll never know…

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:04.379
Kamron Hanson said, “I would take the coffee
machine and the desire camera's powers and

00:12:04.379 --> 00:12:06.890
see what people truly wanna drink lol.”

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:07.890
Well…

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.279
That’s a thought-provoking combination.

00:12:10.279 --> 00:12:14.480
The more I think about it, the more its strange
ambiguity disturbs me.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:19.320
Mincat 1326 said, “I want to be like SCP-001
When Day Breaks.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:26.449
It would be fun to see masses of flesh slithering
around, absorbing more people and animals.”

00:12:26.449 --> 00:12:31.459
All I can say is that you and I have very
different ideas of fun, Mincat…

00:12:31.459 --> 00:12:35.990
Green Koopa said, “I'll be honest...more
than anything in the scp multiverse I want

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.300
to release the Devourer.”

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.779
This isn’t even really a power as much as
it is an odd, self-destructive desire to bring

00:12:42.779 --> 00:12:44.569
about the apocalypse by proxy.

00:12:44.569 --> 00:12:49.600
Wouldn’t it be more fun to have super-strength
or fly than release a monster that’ll eat

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.879
all of humanity - Yourself included?

00:12:51.879 --> 00:12:55.029
I’m just saying, it’s worth considering.

00:12:55.029 --> 00:12:59.550
Sarah Walden said, “I would want powers
like SCP-055 so I could...

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:01.619
wait... why am I here again?”

00:13:01.619 --> 00:13:03.660
That’s a good question.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.029
I think it had something to do with the, um.

00:13:07.029 --> 00:13:08.129
Uh.

00:13:08.129 --> 00:13:12.160
Gimme a second.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:15.100
Uhhhh…

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:19.160
Polygon said, “Personally, I would want
SCP-005.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.790
It feels cool to open any door in existence.”

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:25.980
This would be an excellent ability with a
wide number of applications.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:30.360
But as we learned from Green Koopa and his
aspirations to free the Devourer not long

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:33.559
ago, some doors are just better left closed.

00:13:33.559 --> 00:13:38.100
Jevan Llew Clovis said, “If Dr. Bright doesn't
want his amulet, I can have it.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:42.970
I'm fully aware of the consequences of his
immortality, but I won't alter or change them.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:46.509
I just want to outlive everyone and everything.”

00:13:46.509 --> 00:13:47.879
Is…

00:13:47.879 --> 00:13:49.429
Everything okay, Jevan?

00:13:49.429 --> 00:13:55.029
That’s certainly a frightening, Johan Liebert-esque
aspiration, but I think outliving all other

00:13:55.029 --> 00:13:58.990
life and drifting through the infinite void
of space for an eternity afterwards isn’t

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:01.100
nearly as fun as you might think.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:06.239
WizardShark said, “Probably 5094: I’d
not only be the greatest teacher on the planet

00:14:06.239 --> 00:14:08.230
but I’d also know practically everything.”

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:10.689
A noble ambition, to be sure.

00:14:10.689 --> 00:14:15.160
The world needs great teachers, and it’s
not like Miss J can school everyone.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.730
Some brave anomalous teachers need to take
up the mantle.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:22.749
Knight Fury Productions said, “I’d borrow
the gender-switching stone’s abilities.”

00:14:22.749 --> 00:14:27.589
The gender-switching stone’s abilities would
be undeniably useful, especially for transgender

00:14:27.589 --> 00:14:28.589
people.

00:14:28.589 --> 00:14:32.429
Just make sure you don’t use it on the same
person too many times - There can be some

00:14:32.429 --> 00:14:34.160
nasty side effects.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.389
Bob bert said, “Oh this one is easy, the
tomatoes that kill anyone who makes a terrible

00:14:38.389 --> 00:14:39.389
joke.”

00:14:39.389 --> 00:14:45.550
That would be a dangerous ability to have
in one of these comment-response videos…

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:49.769
Poland fan said, “096 so I can murder anyone
who looks at me.”

00:14:49.769 --> 00:14:54.369
Personally, we’d recommend therapy to get
over this crippling homicidal shyness.

00:14:54.369 --> 00:14:58.420
Though once again, technically, this is also
something you could do without anomalous powers.

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:04.629
We’d just strongly recommend that you don’t
do it, because committing murder is not cool.

00:15:04.629 --> 00:15:10.899
Mr Xtreme said, “I will like to have the
ability of SCP-049, not killing with a touch,

00:15:10.899 --> 00:15:13.839
but actually "curing" this COVID 19 pandemic.

00:15:13.839 --> 00:15:18.139
I prefer to have the power of curing every
person affected by the pandemic by a single

00:15:18.139 --> 00:15:19.420
touch of my hand.”

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:24.310
The real tragedy is that your dream is likely
shared by the Plague Doctor himself.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:29.029
He wishes he could bring life instead of death,
cures instead of corruption, but such a thing

00:15:29.029 --> 00:15:32.410
seems out of the cards for this poor anomalous
doc…

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:37.179
The Christmas Cretin said, “I'd love to
have the abilities of 2786 so I could just

00:15:37.179 --> 00:15:40.329
stay in a book and not exist in the real world
for a fat minute.”

00:15:40.329 --> 00:15:43.370
Honestly, I think we’ve all felt like that
sometimes.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:47.000
But hey, you don’t need anomalous powers
to lose yourself in a great book for a little

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.000
while.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:52.420
We thoroughly recommend trying it, as long
as it’s not an evil book, like the Encyclopedia

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:55.649
of Common Diseases or A Chronicle of the Daevas.

00:15:55.649 --> 00:16:01.560
Addison Peacock said, “I'd love to shapeshift
like SCP-953, spontaneously generate pizza

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:07.600
like 458, or the lifesaving abilities of the
Teddy Bear Doctor 2295.”

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.649
This is a powerful triple threat.

00:16:09.649 --> 00:16:14.220
We’d personally watch a prestige television
drama about a person shapeshifting to live

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:18.269
a double life as an anomalous surgeon and
a world-class pizza chef.

00:16:18.269 --> 00:16:21.499
If any TV executives see this, please get
in contact.

00:16:21.499 --> 00:16:25.370
Though sadly we will need to dose you with
amnestics afterwards.

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:30.490
Lyndsey J. said, “The incredible brand integration
and longevity powers of SCP-3166.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.790
PAWS for ten thousand years.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:41.249
PAWS until the sun is a flickering ember,
and the face of Man is resigned to dust with

00:16:41.249 --> 00:16:42.249
his cities.

00:16:42.249 --> 00:16:52.149
The day when the universe goes cold will be
a Monday.”

00:16:52.149 --> 00:16:57.679
This is so frighteningly on point, part of
me believes that SCP-3166 somehow actually

00:16:57.679 --> 00:16:59.759
wrote this under an alias.

00:16:59.759 --> 00:17:03.579
And if that is the case, we’ll need to dispatch
a Mobile Task Force immediately to make sure

00:17:03.579 --> 00:17:08.570
that Jim Davis, Bill Murray, and all their
many associates are safe from your lasagna-coated

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:09.570
wrath.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:14.510
And there you have it, folks, the most desirable
anomalous abilities among the SCP Explained

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.510
community.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:19.490
For those curious about the overall distribution,
the most commonly requested abilities were

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:26.240
the adaptability of SCP-682, the reality warping
powers of SCP-343, and heartwarmingly, the

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:27.950
positivity powers of SCP-999.

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:31.310
Want to be a part of our next video?

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:35.580
Keep an eye on the community tab, and definitely
let us know which power you’d like to have

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.110
down in the comments.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:40.470
Not because we’re working with Foundation
Field Agents who want to root out possibly

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:44.450
anomalous individuals using our videos to
learn more about their inner workings.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.570
Just because we’re curious.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.570
Honest.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:51.610
Now go check out “SCP-096 - Look at a Picture
of Shy Guy in Space?

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:57.090
The Shy Guy Questions and Theories” and
“How To Actually Beat SCP-3008 The Infinite

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:01.790
Ikea” for more dreams and nightmares from
the fans of SCP Explained!

